-old Earl of Douglas and his  ten year old brother were invited to a  feast with James a second the child king  of Scotland the King's advisers dragged  the young girl and his brothers outside  the castle gave them a mock trial and  then beheaded them both the Lannisters  and there occurred  similarly the purple wedding where King  Joffrey meets his maker was based on a  real incident to the poisoning and death  of England's Prince Eustace at a feast  in 1153 sometimes fans do the work while  Martin created a lush and vibrant Lee  detailed world in A Song of Ice and Fire  he does occasionally leave things out as  a result the showrunners sometimes have  to use their own imaginations or that of  to fill in the gaps in one prominent  example from season six the show's  costumers were tasked with creating a  sigil buckle for Howland Reed to wear  during the Tower of joy flashback scenes  Martha that described it in the books as  an alligator like lizard lion but he  never offered a complete description  luckily fans have been creating artwork  based on Martin's vision for years the  producers must have been impressed with  this image since it sure looks like it  was copied and pasted right onto Reed's  costume horsepower and bodybuilding in  season six during the breathtaking  cavalry charge at the Battle of the  bastards Jon Snow stands alone on the  battlefield as Ramsay Bolton and amber  horsemen right toward him at breakneck  speed but snows army suddenly rushes up  behind him igniting one of the show's  most impressive battle scenes if he  thought it had to be green-screen  trickery however you were wrong the  showrunners revealed in a  behind-the-scenes video that those were  dozens of real-life horses charging  Harrington at full gallop until the last  minute I was stood there facing off  against this cavalry charge which is  really scary we're a bit annoyed because  I think everyone's gonna think it was  CGI and it wasn't so now we know about  the horses but how do producers create  that impressive pile of bodies on the  battlefield during the battle the video  reveals that all the bodies were  actually life-size dummies not  computer-generated fakery the crew  acquired hundreds of mannequins dressed  them in appropriate house umber and  house Bolton armor then coated them in  mud and fake blood and piled them in a  gigantic heap even the dead horses among  the men are dummies equipped with  saddles now that's attention to detail  happy ending for lady one of the most  heartbreaking moments on Game of Thrones  came during season one when Prince  Joffrey orders the death of aiiah Starks  beloved direwolf when the Lannister  soldiers can't locate I as pets Queen  Cersei orders that Sansa style wolf lady  be killed instead thankfully lady or  rather the northern Inuit dog that  played her on-screen  got a happier ending in real life  actress sophie Turner bonded with the  animals and she adopted her more than  meets the eye in A Song of Ice and Fire  Daenerys Targaryen and her brother  Viserys have purple eyes and Game of  Thrones showrunners planned for them to  have them on the show as well  unfortunately the purple contacts  affected actress Emilia Clarke  so badly that producers decided to ditch  the contacts and reshoot the scenes of a  natural baby blues and that's not the  only eye-opening tale from the set i  astark has blinded during her training  with the faceless men and in order to  accurately portray the role actress  Maisie Williams wore completely opaque  sixteen millimeter thick contact lenses  for her speaking scenes and a pair with  only a pinhole in the center during  fight scenes a gift for hate until  Ramsay snow hit the screen during season  3 Joffrey Baratheon was perhaps the most  universally despised character on the  show which I disagree with he was the  best character by far Irish actor Jack  Gleeson did such a convincing job as a  sadistic boy king that Martin reportedly  sent him a note that rea